  "text": "Create and publish digital intake forms for patients\n\nCustom intake questionnaires streamline the check-in process by letting patients submit information securely before arrival.\n\n### Steps to Create and Publish a Form\n1. Go to **Patient Portal > Form Builder**.\n2. Click **New Form** and select a template type, such as *Medical History* or *Consent*.\n3. Drag and drop desired fields into the layout area. Required fields must have the **Mandatory** toggle enabled.\n4. Click **Save Draft**, then select **Publish to Portal**.\n5. Navigate to **Patient Portal > Settings** to assign the form to specific appointment types.\n\n### Limits and Conditions\n- Forms can only be published if all required field validation checks pass without errors.\n- Patients must have an active portal account to receive and complete assigned questionnaires.\n- Maximum file upload size within a single form is 25 MB.\n\n### Troubleshooting\nIf form fields trigger validation errors upon publication, check for duplicate field IDs or unassigned dropdown options. Clear your browser cache and reload **Form Builder** if changes do not appear on the live patient portal immediately. Contact support if validation errors persist after correcting all flagged items."
 },
